<?php
return ['name' => 'attuned_ji_earth_the_cultivator', 'displayTitle' => ['en' => 'Attuned Ji Earth – The Cultivator', 'zh' => '身弱己土'], 'locales' => ['en' => ['sections' => ['overview' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<p>Attuned Ji Earth is the soil of a humble field – not grand or imposing like a mountain, but rich with quiet potential. When its energy is in a \'weak\' phase, it might have limited strength or influence and requires careful tending (through experience, knowledge, and support) to build itself up. However, its value doesn\'t come from dominating the landscape; it comes from the ability to nurture life\'s everyday growth. It understands that even the plainest earth can harbor incredible vitality. It works steadily in the background, ensuring that projects, people, and ideas around it get the nourishment they need to thrive continuously. As The Cultivator, it focuses on developing and supporting every possibility in its environment. With unwavering patience and stability, Attuned Ji Earth becomes an irreplaceable source of sustenance – the one that helps ideas take root, relationships grow stronger, and dreams come to fruition, all without seeking the spotlight for itself.</p><p>Gentle & Accommodating: You are warm-hearted and approach others with patience and kindness. In both personal and work settings, you\'re the one who listens, mediates, and finds common ground. You\'re excellent at coordinating among different people and making everyone feel heard. This gives those around you a deep sense of comfort and trust in you. The flip side is that you may sometimes yield too much – in trying to make everyone else happy, you might suppress your own needs or opinions. Remember, your voice matters too.<br/>Cautious & Sensitive: Internally, you\'re quite sensitive and often worry about worst-case scenarios. Security is very important to you – you like to know the plan, the backup plan, and maybe have a backup for the backup. This makes you incredibly prepared and rarely caught off guard. But life doesn\'t always allow for perfect security; there are times when your excessive caution or fear of what could go wrong might cause you to miss out on exciting opportunities. Learning to occasionally take a leap of faith is a challenge worth tackling for you.<br/>Principled & Steadfast: You come across as easygoing, maybe even submissive or very flexible, and indeed you prefer harmony over conflict. Yet, there\'s a line in the sand that you won\'t cross – core principles or values you uphold firmly. When someone or something violates what you believe is right (or jeopardizes those you care about), you reveal a surprisingly firm backbone. In those moments, you\'ll stand up and hold your ground with quiet strength, no matter the pressure to yield.</p>'], 'love' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<p>Fire, Earth. As an Attuned Ji Earth, you sometimes feel a lack of the natural confidence or push that stronger personalities have. To bolster yourself, embrace Fire and Earth energies around you. Fire adds passion, motivation, and warmth – it gives you that spark to get moving and assert yourself when needed. Being around enthusiastic, positive people or engaging in creative hobbies can ignite this Fire within. Additional Earth (yes, your own element) in a supportive way – like spending time in nature, maintaining a stable routine, or seeking mentorship from reliable figures – will reinforce your sense of security and resilience. By combining Fire\'s dynamism with Earth\'s steadiness, you\'ll gradually build more inner strength and courage, giving you greater assurance in executing your plans and tackling challenges.</p>'], 'career' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<h4>Wealth</h4><p>You are not particularly drawn to solo ventures or aggressive financial competition, and that\'s perfectly fine. In fact, teaming up often brings you luck in finances. Partnerships, cooperative projects, or family businesses can be profitable avenues for you. Early in life, you might rely on support or resources from family/mentors to get started, and there\'s no shame in that – you have a karma of benefiting from group endeavors and collective support. As you progress into mid-life, you\'ll likely find your financial situation improving steadily, thanks to years of careful saving, incremental investing, and maybe climbing the ladder in a secure job. Continue to be cautious with money: avoid high-risk bets, speculative trades, or taking out large loans. Debt, especially, could cause you more stress than it\'s worth, so stick to what you can afford and grow slowly. By the second half of your career, you\'ll probably have built a comfortable nest egg, and your challenge will shift from accumulating wealth to preserving it. Diversify into safe investments, perhaps some real estate for rental income or bonds for interest – nothing flashy, just good old stability. Also, consider insurance and rainy-day funds for peace of mind. With your natural inclination to plan ahead, you\'ll likely enter retirement with solid security and maybe even be the financial rock for your extended family, ensuring everyone is taken care of.</p><h4>Health</h4><p>Keeping your digestion robust continues to be a theme. Regular, balanced meals do wonders for your mood and energy level. Try not to skip breakfast or eat dinner too late; your body likes a rhythm. Be mindful of emotional eating as well – if you get anxious, you might gravitate towards comfort foods (sweets, carbs, etc.), but these can upset your stomach and create a vicious cycle of discomfort and anxiety. Instead, find healthier comfort foods (like warm herbal teas, oatmeal, or soup) that soothe both your stomach and nerves. Speaking of nerves, your skin might act as an emotional barometer. Under stress, you could experience breakouts, rashes, or other skin flare-ups. To mitigate this, avoid overly spicy or \'heaty\' foods which, in traditional terms, can trigger inflammation. Keep your skin routine gentle: moisturize, protect from harsh weather, and don\'t over-cleanse – your skin needs its natural oils to stay healthy. Also, indulge in relaxation techniques that directly calm the body: a warm bath with Epsom salts, a calming skincare ritual at night, or gentle self-massage. When your body feels safe and cared for, your mind will follow. Overall, your health will flourish with consistency: consistent sleep (try to keep a regular bedtime), consistent moderate exercise (like a daily walk or yoga session to keep your circulation and muscles in shape), and consistent check-ins with yourself emotionally so that stress doesn\'t silently accumulate.</p><h4>Emotional Wellbeing</h4><p>Your emotional default is to worry – often quietly, without letting others know – and to carry more than your share of responsibilities on your shoulders. To maintain your emotional equilibrium, it\'s vital to stay grounded and connected to simple joys. Long walks in nature, tending to a small garden, or even casual hiking on a trail can give you a peaceful release. The act of walking, especially, is like a moving meditation for you: each step is methodical and reassuring, symbolically reminding you that life progresses one step at a time (and that\'s okay). Another wonderful outlet is any activity that involves working gently with your hands and the earth. Pottery was mentioned before and is great – likewise, baking bread, knitting, or painting can be therapeutic. The key is to engage in something where results come from slow, patient effort. As you see a plant grow or a craft project take shape over days or weeks, you internalize the lesson that progress is being made, even if it\'s not instantaneous. This realization helps combat feelings of anxiety about the future. Finally, don\'t hesitate to lean on your support network for emotional sustenance. Have tea or coffee regularly with a friend who understands you or keep a journal where you can pour out thoughts without judgment. These practices will till the soil of your mind, keeping it fertile and light, rather than heavy with unspoken worries.</p><h4>Career Pathways</h4><p>Where You Flourish: Education: You are well-suited for roles in education that require dedication and compassion. You could be an excellent elementary or high school teacher, patiently guiding the next generation. Special education is another area where your empathy and steadiness would shine, helping students with unique needs grow at their own pace. Additionally, you might enjoy working in adult education or vocational training programs, where you can help others develop practical skills through consistent practice and support. Online education is booming and could also be a realm for you – perhaps as a curriculum planner or online tutor, bringing structured learning to many. Cultural Preservation & Media: Careers in libraries, archives, museums, or cultural research fit your careful, methodical style. As a librarian or archivist, you would manage information with precision and help preserve knowledge for future generations. In a museum or as a cultural historian/archaeologist, you would engage in the slow, meticulous work of studying and curating exhibits or data that enrich our understanding of the past. You could also thrive in publishing – perhaps as an editor or content curator – ensuring that quality work gets polished and seen by the world. Consulting & Social Services: You have a natural ability to help and organize, which can translate into roles like a counselor, social worker, or community service coordinator. In counseling (be it psychological, academic, or career counseling), your patient listening and step-by-step guidance can make a real difference in people\'s lives. In social work or community services, you\'d be the steady force that coordinates aid, manages casework, and follows through on helping those in need, even when it involves a lot of paperwork or slow progress – you don\'t lose heart easily, and that\'s crucial in these fields. Scientific Research & QA: If you\'re drawn to science or tech, consider behind-the-scenes roles that require diligence. You might become a reliable lab technician, a data scientist ensuring the integrity of datasets, a database manager keeping information systems stable, or a software tester/quality assurance engineer meticulously checking programs for bugs. While others may find these tasks tedious, you take pride in thoroughness. Your contributions in these roles are the backbone that allows big discoveries and innovations to stand on solid ground. Infrastructure & Urban Development: Working in city planning, civil engineering, or property management can also be fulfilling. For instance, as a civil engineer or construction project manager, you\'d be literally building and maintaining the physical world, brick by brick. It\'s steady, tangible work that improves people\'s lives – building roads, schools, homes – and you\'ll excel at coordinating the many small details and plans required. Similarly, as a property or facilities manager, you\'d keep buildings running smoothly with preventative maintenance and careful scheduling, something very much in line with your style. Hospitality & Culinary Arts: Don\'t underestimate fields like hotel management, bakery/pastry arts, or tea/coffee curation. These are industries where providing consistent comfort and quality, day in and day out, is key to success. You could run a charming bed-and-breakfast where guests feel at home thanks to your thoughtful touches, or you might excel as a pastry chef, patiently perfecting recipes and delighting people with your creations. Even being a tea sommelier or cafe owner, where you cultivate a warm atmosphere and a dependable routine, could bring you joy and success. Public Administration & Energy Sector: A stable government job or a role in public utilities (electric, gas, water, renewable energy) might suit you. The bureaucratic pace, which some find stifling, can actually be a comfort for you – clear rules, job security, and the knowledge that your work contributes to the greater good. Within these sectors, you could work on long-term projects like urban housing schemes, environmental conservation programs, or energy infrastructure planning, applying your methodical approach to create sustainable, long-lasting improvements. Where Energy Feels Drained: Fashion & Trend-Driven Industries: Fast fashion, trend marketing, or social media influencing often require you to constantly adapt to new fads and put yourself out there energetically. The rapid turnover and external validation cycle in these industries can be exhausting and unfulfilling for someone who prefers substance over style. Jobs like fashion buyer, trend analyst, or viral content creator might leave you feeling ungrounded and stressed. Aquatic & Adventure Careers: Commercial fishing, cruise hospitality, adventure tourism (like being a safari or mountain guide), or sailing jobs introduce a high level of unpredictability – from weather to customer behavior. While you love nature, making a career out of navigating its wild, uncontrollable side (especially over water) could be overwhelming. Such careers demand quick reflexes and risk-taking that don\'t align with your careful planning. High-Speed Transportation: Roles like air traffic controller, pilot, or emergency logistics responder come with split-second decisions and high stakes under pressure. The constant adrenaline and immediate problem-solving required could burn you out and spike your anxiety. You function better in an environment where you can double-check and methodically approach problems rather than one where you must be rapid-fire all the time. Speculative Finance & Arbitration: Being a stockbroker, hedge fund trader, or venture capitalist involves big gambles and handling potential failures regularly. Similarly, a career as a trial lawyer or arbitrator in frequent high-conflict scenarios might wear on you. These jobs are adversarial and uncertain by nature, which could chip away at your inner peace. You\'re more at ease in collaborative or at least stable, rule-governed settings. Horticulture Business Leadership: While you connect with nature, running a large commercial horticulture or floristry enterprise (with all the business negotiations, marketing, and volatile market demand that entails) may not suit you. It combines the pressures of entrepreneurship with the unpredictability of agriculture and consumer trends. You\'d likely prefer working in such an industry in a stable role (like as an expert gardener or a consultant) rather than being the one who has to constantly hustle and expand the business under pressure.</p>'], 'relationship_friends' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>Bing Fire: A Bing Fire friend illuminates your life with enthusiasm and positivity. Whenever you feel down or unmotivated, they have a knack for warming your heart and energizing you. They\'ll crack jokes to lift your spirits or drag you out on a fun outing when you\'re inclined to stay home worrying.</li><li>Wu Earth: A Wu Earth friend (with a stronger constitution) complements you perfectly. This friend is solid and dependable, much like you, but likely has a bit more assertiveness. Together, you form a team that can face difficulties head-on.</li></ul>'], 'relationship_couple' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>Wu Earth: A Wu Earth partner is the quintessential \'strong and silent\' type who is deeply trustworthy. In a relationship with you, they handle many practical burdens with you or on your behalf, allowing you to feel secure. They won\'t run at the first sign of trouble.</li><li>Geng Metal: A Geng Metal partner brings a breath of fresh air into your life by challenging some of your more conservative or anxious tendencies. They are straightforward and often fearless in expressing themselves, which can help coax you out of overthinking.</li></ul>'], 'celebrities_international' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>Maria Montessori: An Italian educator who revolutionized early childhood education with the Montessori method, which emphasizes child-led, hands-on learning at a gentle pace. Her approach was not about forcing outcomes, but about nurturing each child\'s potential</li></ul>'], 'celebrities_domestic' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>Mo Yan: A Nobel Prize-winning Chinese author known for his rich storytelling rooted in his rural upbringing. He spent years honing his craft, writing about the lives of ordinary people with great empathy and depth</li></ul>'], 'lucksuggestion_dailytips' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>Bedside Warmth: Place a soft, warm-glow lamp by your bedside and turn it on in the evening. The gentle light will help soothe your mind as you wind down. It\'s more than decor – it\'s a ritual. As that warm light fills your room, take a few moments to reflect on the day\'s small accomplishments (e.g., \'I helped a colleague,\' \'I cooked a nice meal\'). This practice can improve your sense of security and contentment, reinforcing the idea that each day you are steadily cultivating something good</li><li>Soak Up the Sun: Make it a point to get some natural sunlight every day, especially in the morning if possible. Whether it\'s enjoying your breakfast by a sunny window or taking a short walk during a break, sunlight will lift your mood and energize your Earth element. It boosts your metabolism, strengthens your immunity, and even helps regulate sleep – all things that keep you in balance. Think of yourself as a plant, and the sun is nourishment; a little dose each day helps you flourish</li></ul>'], 'lucksuggestion_color' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>Yellow (Earth): Sunny, golden hues are your personal energizer. Yellow reinforces your resilience and optimism, acting almost like a shield against stress. Wearing a touch of yellow – be it a scarf, tie, socks, or even using a yellow mug at work – can remind you of your own strength and brighten your disposition. Decorate your personal space with a dash of yellow (maybe throw pillows or a wall accent) to create a comforting atmosphere. This color grounds you deeply, helping you stay calm and composed under pressure.</li><li>Red & Purple (Fire): These passionate colors inject you with dynamism and confidence. When you have an important task or you\'re facing a situation where you need an extra push, surround yourself with red or purple. It could be as simple as using a red pen, carrying a purple notebook, or putting on a piece of garnet or amethyst jewelry. Red ignites your determination, and purple inspires courage and creativity. The mix of both can spur you into action when you\'d otherwise hesitate, ensuring you seize opportunities at critical moments. Use them as accents in moderation – a little Fire goes a long way to keep you motivated and on track.</li></ul>'], 'lucksuggestion_location' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>Southwest (Earth): Southwest is your power spot. It\'s associated with stability, relationships, and the nurturing Earth energy you resonate with. Spending time facing southwest – for example, positioning your favorite chair or your work desk toward the SW – can subtly increase your sense of security and rootedness. It\'s a great direction to face when you\'re doing something restorative, like reading or enjoying a cup of tea, as it magnifies that restorative effect and helps replenish your inner strength.</li><li>South (Fire): The south direction infuses you with drive and enthusiasm. When you need to be proactive or tackle a \'to-do\' list efficiently, try facing south or arranging to be in a south-end room. This direction\'s vibrancy fights off any sluggishness or doubt, giving you a gentle energetic boost. In meetings or presentations, if you have any control over seating, sitting on the southern side of the table/room can psychologically bolster your assertiveness and presence. Essentially, South lights a little fire under you, helping you be more active, upbeat, and effective in whatever you set out to do.</li></ul>']]], 'zh' => ['sections' => ['overview' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<p>己土为田园之土，身弱则力量有限，需要精心耕耘才能稳固成长。它的价值不在于高山般巍峨，而在于在平凡中孕育生命，默默滋养周围。</p><p>温和包容：性情温和，处事细致耐心，擅长协调关系，给人踏实可靠之感。<br/>谨慎敏感：内在敏感多虑，重视安全感，行事谨慎保守，易因过度担忧而错失机遇。<br/>坚守原则：表面柔顺，但涉及原则问题时，会显露出固执坚韧的一面。</p>'], 'love' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<p>身弱己土，喜用神为火、土。己土如田园之土，身弱时容易缺乏稳定感和内在支撑。</p>'], 'career' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<h4>财富运势</h4><p>不适合自己单打独斗，适合通过合作、长辈资源获利，中年后财运佳，避免投机或借贷。</p><h4>健康隐患</h4><p>调理脾胃，保持规律饮食，避免暴饮暴食，少吃油腻和辛辣食物；注意皮肤问题，避免刺激性食物，注意保湿。</p><h4>情绪管理</h4><p>内心易产生焦虑情绪，可通过徒步、陶艺等接地气活动舒缓心神。</p><h4>职业管理</h4><p>推荐行业：教育：学校、培训机构、教育咨询。文化传播：出版社、文化传媒、广告公司。心理咨询：心理治疗、心理辅导、心理健康。行政管理：行政事务、人事管理、办公管理。仓储物流：物流管理、仓储运营、供应链。财务审计：会计师事务所、财务管理、审计服务。慎重行业：园艺花艺：园艺设计、花卉种植、花店经营。销售：销售代理、商业销售、客户服务。创意策划：广告策划、活动策划、创意设计。导游：旅游服务、景点讲解、文化旅游。直播娱乐：直播平台、娱乐主播、数字娱乐。风险投资：金融投资、创业投资、股权投资。</p>'], 'relationship_friends' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>丙火：丙火会给你带来温暖能量，驱散阴郁。</li><li>戊土：戊土能够和你一起面对困难，帮你承担压力。</li></ul>'], 'relationship_couple' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>戊土：戊土作为伴侣踏实可靠，可以与你共同承担家庭责任。</li><li>庚金：庚金可以打破你保守固执的一面，化解你的多思多虑。</li></ul>'], 'celebrities_international' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>Maria Montessori：创立蒙特梭利教育法，强调儿童自主学习</li></ul>'], 'celebrities_domestic' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>莫言：诺贝尔文学奖得主</li></ul>'], 'lucksuggestion_dailytips' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>床头可以放一盏暖光灯</li><li>多晒太阳</li></ul>'], 'lucksuggestion_color' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>黄色（土）：黄色象征稳固与根基，能增强抗压能力。</li><li>红色 / 紫色（火）：红色带来热情，紫色象征灵感与果敢，能激发行动力。</li></ul>'], 'lucksuggestion_location' => ['title' => '', 'content' => '<ul><li>西南方（土）：西南方的能量象征稳定与根基，能增强内在稳固性。</li><li>南方（火）：南方的能量象征动力与热情，能增强行动力。</li></ul>']]]], 'version' => 1];
